# candidate T17 Change 2 -- honest_z accumulates IN PLACE
#   ring::mul_short_add_into writes straight into the accumulator, and
#   honest_z holds a bare Vec<Rq> so both branches can write into it.
#   Removes, per message block at the pin: the per-column product's two
#   allocations (8192 x 2), the 8192-element column vector (64 MiB), and
#   the vector add's result (another 64 MiB) -- plus ~16.7M pushes.
# champion = Change 1 (committed 6dff292). Evidence = the two short
#   rows; honest_z_dense is the fallback guard (must not read slower).
# Gated on IDLE CPU, not load average: after a heavy build the 1-minute
#   load EMA stays above 3 for many minutes while the machine is 80%+
#   idle, so a load gate waits for nothing. The serial-bench rule is
#   enforced separately by the cargo/lean checks.
